// Round 75 ADDS rows rather than regenerating the file: round 24's source
// upload folders are long gone, so re-running it would produce eighteen
// missing-folder errors and no manifest at all. Both scripts write the same
// row shape through the same build() -- see extract_round75_creatures.py,
// which imports round 24 rather than reimplementing it.
//
// Sheet geometry for all 15 monster families. Every atlas is laid out rows =
// SHADES, columns = (direction, frame):
//   frame = shadeRow * (8 * framesPerDir) + dirCol * framesPerDir + step
// which is the convention every previous round's monster atlas already used,
// so this added a third state (attack) without changing how any of them are
// indexed.
//
// `cell` is measured, not chosen: each family is packed into the tightest
// square that holds every frame of every state, which is what makes five
// shades of three animations fit in roughly the memory two animations used
// to take. `displayScale` is derived from the on-screen height the creature
// should read at, so a family keeps its intended size no matter what
// resolution it happened to ship at.
